※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4436 LANG_TUPLE_NOT_A_TUPLE

※ Names written next to each other take a tuple apart.  A value that is not
※ one is the one value it is, and there is nothing in it for a second name to
※ stand for.

let n: mut u8 = 3u8

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let a, b := n
    a + b
